    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm having an issue with some walnut I'm working with for a cabinet project. I'm cutting dovetails by hand, but I keep getting these small splinters and tear-outs right at the tips of the pins. It's ruining the fit. Any idea what I might be doing wrong with my chisel or my grain direction?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This issue often comes down to how you are attacking the grain, especially with dense wood like walnut. Try ensuring your chisel is razor-sharp, as dull edges tear rather than slice the wood fibers cleanly. Also, always ensure your bevel is slightly angled *with* the grain when paring down the shoulders of the tails or pins to encourage a smoother cut.",
      "source": "target",
